			"notes": "## Adaptive Server Core (ASC) v1.0.1\n\nThis patch release addresses critical performance issues reported under high-speed player traversal (Elytra flights and player scattering), resolves player skin layer rendering desynchronization, eliminates main-thread database micro-freezes, and enhances the in-game Admin GUI.\n\n### 🐛 Critical Bug Fixes\n- **Player Skin Layer Desync**:\n  - View distance and simulation distance updates are now strictly dispatched synchronously on the main tick thread (`scheduler.runSync`), preserving clientbound entity tracking bitmasks (jacket, sleeves, pant legs).\n  - Added hysteresis damping to prevent view distance flapping under fluctuating loads.\n- **Elytra Gliding & Fast Scatter Chunk Stalls**:\n  - Filtered `PlayerMoveEvent` with early exit for non-gliding players to eliminate computation overhead during normal movement.\n  - Rate-limited Elytra trajectory evaluation to at most once per 500ms per player.\n  - Added `inFlightChunks` deduplication registry to stop spamming duplicate requests to Paper's `ChunkTaskScheduler`.\n- **Console Log Spam & Micro-Freezes**:\n  - Replaced synchronous SQLite JDBC operations on chunk unload with an O(1) in-memory buffer and a dedicated background daemon flusher committing batches every 5 seconds.\n  - Resolved `SQLITE_BUSY` database lock warnings and 10–50ms main thread pauses.\n- **World Generation Spawns**:\n  - Excluded `CHUNK_GEN` spawn reason from mob cap throttling so newly generated chunk animals are never blocked.\n\n### 🎨 In-Game Admin GUI Enhancements\n- **Click Protection**: Implemented `ASCGuiHolder` across all server platforms to prevent items from being picked up or moved.\n- **Intuitive Icons & Dedicated Switches**:\n  - MobCap (`SPAWNER`), Redstone (`REPEATER`), Chunk/Elytra (`ELYTRA`), LazySim (`FURNACE`).\n  - Added individual green (`LIME_CONCRETE`) and red (`RED_CONCRETE`) toggle switches underneath each module.\n\n### 📦 Assets Included\n- `AdaptiveServerCore-Universal.jar` (Recommended universal jar with runtime platform auto-detection)\n- `AdaptiveServerCore-Paper-1.21.jar` (Paper 1.21+ and Folia)\n- `AdaptiveServerCore-Paper-Legacy.jar` (Paper 1.16–1.19)\n- `AdaptiveServerCore-Spigot.jar` (Spigot fallback)\n- `AdaptiveServerCore-Bukkit.jar` (Bukkit baseline)"
		},
